(1) As evidence of the reliability and professional suitability of an agent, an institution must, for the purposes of § 25(2) sentence 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz, obtain at least:
1. a current certificate of good conduct for the managing directors of the agent and for the persons responsible for its management (§ 30(1) of the Bundeszentralregistergesetz);
2. a current extract from the Gewerbezentralregister (§§ 149, 150 of the Gewerbeordnung) for the agent, the managing directors of the agent and the persons responsible for its management;
3. a current extract from the register of debtors under § 882b of the Zivilprozessordnung for the agent, the managing directors of the agent and the persons responsible for its management;
4. declarations of the managing directors of the agent and of the persons responsible for its management, and the related documents, in accordance with § 10(1) of the ZAG-Anzeigenverordnung;
5. a current tax compliance certificate from the Finanzamt for the agent, the managing directors of the agent and the persons responsible for its management;
6. current information from the trade authority under § 14 of the Gewerbeordnung for the agent;
7. a current extract from the commercial register for the agent;
8. the most recent annual accounts or the most recent statement of income over expenditure of the agent and a current business evaluation;
9. current certificates of registration of residence for the managing directors of the agent and for the persons responsible for its management;
10. complete curricula vitae, signed by hand, of the managing directors of the agent and of the persons responsible for its management, setting out all education and training and all professional and commercial activities;
11. the customary evidence of the activities and performance for the education and training and the professional and commercial activities stated in the curriculum vitae under point 10;
12. evidence of the official approvals and permits that are required according to the activities stated in the curriculum vitae under point 10 and the trade registration under point 6.
The institution must actively follow up and clarify any incompleteness, defects and contradictions in the documents and particulars submitted by the agent or obtained for the managing directors of the agent or for the responsible persons. Where necessary, further evidence must be obtained. For agents within the meaning of § 25(4) of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz, comparable information from authorities must be obtained where it is issued in the State in which the agent is established. Where the law of the State in which the agent is established provides for further evidence under Article 19(1)(c) of Directive (EU) 2015/2366 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 25 November 2015 on payment services in the internal market, amending Directives 2002/65/EC, 2009/110/EC and 2013/36/EU and Regulation (EU) No 1093/2010, and repealing Directive 2007/64/EC (OJ L 337, 23.12.2015, p. 35; L 169, 28.6.2016, p. 18; L 102, 23.4.2018, p. 97; L 126, 23.5.2018, p. 10), that evidence must also be obtained.

(2) Professional suitability requires evidence that the agent has sufficient theoretical and practical knowledge of the payment services to be provided.

