(1) The institutions liable to pay contributions under § 2 sentence 1 points 1 and 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz, with the exception of the institutions referred to in § 1(1) of this Regulation, are required to transmit to the resolution authority the particulars necessary to determine the risk indicators under § 5 of this Regulation. This obligation applies in addition to the reporting obligations under Article 14(2) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 and under §§ 3 and 4 of this Regulation. Article 14(6) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 applies accordingly. For the reference year of the annual accounts referred to in Article 14(1) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63, the following data in particular must be transmitted in each case:
1. asset item No 6a “trading portfolio” and liability item No 3a “trading portfolio” from Form 1 of the Kreditinstituts-Rechnungslegungsverordnung;
2. item No 1 below the line “contingent liabilities” and item No 2 below the line “other commitments” from Form 1 of the Kreditinstituts-Rechnungslegungsverordnung;
3. the notional volume of the forward transactions included under § 36 of the Kreditinstituts-Rechnungslegungsverordnung in the notes to the annual accounts as at the balance sheet date of the relevant reference year;
4. the share of derivatives cleared through a central counterparty;
5. the name of the institutional protection scheme of which the institution is a member, and information on the permission to apply Article 113(7) of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013;
6. for institutions belonging to a group that underwent a reorganisation after receiving state or comparable funds, for example from a resolution financing arrangement, and that is still in the process of reorganisation or resolution, the end date for implementing the reorganisation plan;
7. for institutions that are in liquidation after receiving state or comparable funds, for example from a resolution financing arrangement, the duration of the liquidation plan.

(2) The institutions liable to pay contributions under § 1(1) and (2) must transmit to the resolution authority, for the reference year of the annual accounts referred to in Article 14(1) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63, in particular the following data at the level of individual undertakings in each case:
1. total liabilities within the meaning of point (11) of the second sentence of Article 3 of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63, taking into account § 1(5);
2. the amount of covered deposits within the meaning of point (10) of the second sentence of Article 3 of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63, taking into account § 1(4) and (5);
3. the amount of own funds under § 1(4) and (5).
Article 14(3) and (5) and Article 17(1), (3) and (4) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 apply accordingly.

(3) The resolution authority may also communicate to the institutions liable to pay contributions under § 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz the requirements for transmitting the information under Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 and under this Regulation by publishing them on its website.

(4) The institutions liable to pay contributions under § 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz must confirm to the resolution authority the factual and arithmetical accuracy of the information to be transmitted under Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 and under subsections (1), (2) and (7).

(5) The resolution authority may additionally require institutions liable to pay contributions under § 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz that do not fall under the arrangements for small institutions under Article 10 of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 or that do not pay an annual contribution under § 1(3) of this Regulation to have a statutory auditor confirm the factual and arithmetical accuracy of the information that those institutions must transmit to the resolution authority. In the case of a cooperative or of an incorporated commercial association, the auditing association under § 340k(2) and (2a) of the Handelsgesetzbuch, and in the case of a savings bank, the auditing office of a Sparkassen- und Giroverband under § 340k(3) of the Handelsgesetzbuch, takes the place of the statutory auditor.

(6) The resolution authority may require additional evidence from the institution liable to pay contributions under § 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz in order to verify the particulars provided by that institution or to obtain a basis for a necessary estimate under Article 17(1) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63; it may in particular require the submission of detailed statements of individual calculation items, the accuracy of which must be confirmed by the institution liable to pay contributions.

(7) Where the institutions liable to pay contributions under § 2 of the Restrukturierungsfondsgesetz cannot submit the annual accounts for the reference year under Article 14(1) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 because they were not yet operating at that time, the contribution is calculated on the basis of projected balance sheets for the contribution period concerned. The resolution authority may require these new institutions to submit a projected balance sheet for each contribution period. To the extent that the items and indicators required for calculating the annual contribution are not apparent from the projected balance sheet, the institution must estimate them and transmit them to the resolution authority.

(8) The time limits under Article 14(4) and (5) and Article 20(3) of Delegated Regulation (EU) No 2015/63 apply accordingly to the transmission to the resolution authority of the information under subsections (1), (2) and (7) and of the confirmations under subsections (4) and (5).

