(1) For payment services under § 1(1) sentence 2 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz, for the issuance of electronic money under § 1(2) sentence 2 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz and for other business, the particulars in the accounts must each be shown separately. The items of the balance sheet and of the profit and loss account must be subdivided in accordance with the forms according to whether they derive from payment services, from the issuance of electronic money or from other activities.

(2) The following must each be shown separately as sub-items in Form 1:
1. securitised and non-securitised claims on affiliated undertakings under the items “Claims on credit institutions” (asset item 2), “Claims on customers” (asset item 3), “Claims on institutions within the meaning of § 1(3) of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz” (asset item 4) and “Debt securities and other fixed-income securities” (asset item 5);
2. securitised and non-securitised claims on undertakings with which a participating interest exists, under the items “Claims on credit institutions” (asset item 2), “Claims on customers” (asset item 3), “Claims on institutions within the meaning of § 1(3) of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz” (asset item 4) and “Debt securities and other fixed-income securities” (asset item 5);
3. securitised and non-securitised liabilities to affiliated undertakings under the items “Liabilities to credit institutions” (liability item 1), “Liabilities to customers” (liability item 2), “Liabilities to institutions within the meaning of § 1(3) of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz” (liability item 3) and “Subordinated liabilities” (liability item 8);
4. securitised and non-securitised liabilities to undertakings with which a participating interest exists, under the items “Liabilities to credit institutions” (liability item 1), “Liabilities to customers” (liability item 2), “Liabilities to institutions within the meaning of § 1(3) of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz” (liability item 3) and “Subordinated liabilities” (liability item 8).
The particulars under sentence 1 may be given in the notes, in the order of the items concerned, instead of in the balance sheet.

