The notes must include a list of the types of foreign currency, interest-rate and other forward transactions not yet settled at the balance sheet date that involve only a settlement risk and currency, interest-rate and/or other market price risks from open positions and, in the event of a counterparty default, also from closed positions. These include:
1. forward transactions in foreign currencies, in particular forward foreign exchange transactions, foreign exchange futures, currency swaps, interest rate/currency swaps, obligations as writer of foreign exchange options, foreign exchange option rights, forward transactions in gold and other precious metals, precious metal futures, obligations as writer of gold options, gold option rights;
2. interest-rate forward transactions, in particular forward transactions in fixed-income securities, interest rate futures, forward rate agreements, obligations as writer of interest rate options, interest rate option rights, interest rate swaps, obligations to take up forward forward deposits; delivery obligations arising from such transactions must be noted in the balance sheet sub-item “Irrevocable loan commitments” (liability item 1 below the line);
3. forward transactions with other price risks, in particular equity forward transactions, obligations as writer of share options, share option rights, index futures, obligations as writer of index options, index option rights.
For each of the three breakdown items of forward transactions, it must be stated whether a substantial part of them was concluded to hedge against fluctuations in interest rates, exchange rates or market prices and whether a substantial part of them relates to trading activities.
